Shared state is a Pydantic \texttt{AgentState} (hashes, features, drift flags, \texttt{evaluation\_metrics}, \texttt{drift\_pre\_metrics}, \texttt{pending\_drift\_log}).



\section{Methodology}



\subsection{Autonomous Data Collection \& Agent Tools}

Table~\ref{tab:provenance} separates dynamic collection from fixed configuration. The agent utilizes reusable tools to autonomously search, fetch, validate, and update data streams. If structured APIs (MalwareBazaar, ThreatFox) hit rate limits or fail, the agent dynamically generates CTI web searches to extract fresh indicators of compromise (IOCs). 



\begin{table}[h]

\centering

\caption{Data provenance}

\label{tab:provenance}

\begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{}}

\toprule

\textbf{Dynamic (runtime)} & \textbf{Hardcoded / curated} \\

\midrule

MalwareBazaar / ThreatFox API discovery & Bootstrap malware provider pin (MalwareBazaar) \\

Dynamic CTI feed discovery (web search) & Curated native CTI seed list \\

Dynamic CTI hash extraction from public pages & \texttt{GITHUB\_BENIGN\_REPOS} allowlist \\

Sysinternals directory scrape & CTI download domain allowlist \\

SQLite tracker labels from provider metadata & Optional \texttt{data/benign/} if env enabled \\

\bottomrule

\end{tabular}

\end{table}



\subsection{Feature Engineering}

The pipeline extracts static PE features, including raw header metadata, import table hashing, string distributions, and section entropy. Specifically, the average section entropy is isolated as a primary indicator for our ADWIN drift monitor.



\subsection{Model \& Evaluation}

The system utilizes a LightGBM classifier with Optuna tuning. The baseline model is evaluated across multiple metrics: Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and a specifically constrained False Positive Rate (FPR $\leq 0.1\%$ target). We employ chronological train/val/test splits to maintain strict temporal boundaries (TESSERACT methodology), ensuring older data is never evaluated on newer models.



\subsection{Continual Learning}

\textbf{Bootstrap Phase:} Repeated graph passes until $\geq 100$ malware and $\geq 100$ benign trainable samples exist; drift monitoring is disabled to establish a baseline.

\textbf{Steady State \& Drift:} River ADWIN calculates drift on mean section entropy alongside rolling multivariate shifts on selected features. Upon drift detection, MADAR replay retraining is triggered to update the model using the newly accumulated features mixed with a historical replay budget to prevent catastrophic forgetting.



\section{Results}



\subsection{Performance Over Time}

